@end menu

@node Naming Conventions
@section Naming Conventions

In SCI, variable names use @code{case-insensitive} naming. The frontend normalizes
identifiers to @code{PascalCase} format internally:

@table @asis
@item Input: @code{hello_world}
@*
Output (AST): @code{HelloWorld}

@item Input: @code{MyVariable}
@*
Output (AST): @code{MyVariable}

@item Input: @code{x}
@*
Output (AST): @code{X} (capitalized when unambiguous)

@item Input: @code{_private}
@*
Output (AST): @code{Private}
@end table

All keywords are case-insensitive and conventionally written in lowercase.

@node Lexical Elements
@section Lexical Elements

@subsection Keywords

The following keywords are recognized (case-insensitive):

@table @asis
@item @code{if}
Starts a conditional statement.
@item @code{else}
Specifies the false branch of an IF statement.
@item @code{then}
Separates condition from branch in IF.
@item @code{while}
Starts a while loop.
@item @code{for}
Starts a for loop.
@item @code{foreach}
Iterates over collection elements.
@item @code{break}
Exits the innermost loop immediately.
@item @code{continue}
Skips to the next iteration of the current loop.
@item @code{return}
Returns from a subroutine.
@item @code{define}
Defines a procedure.
@item @code{setq}
Sets a variable to a value.
@item @code{set}
Sets a value (synonym for setq).
@item @code{get}
Gets a property or array element.
@item @code{put}
Puts a value to a property or array element.
@item @code{call}
Calls a procedure.
@item @code{proc}
Procedure definition keyword.
@item @code{method}
Method definition keyword.
@item @code{class}
Class definition keyword.
@item @code{instance}
Instance creation keyword.
@item @code{send}
Message passing to objects.
@item @code{super}
Refers to superclass method.
@item @code{self}
Refers to current object instance.
@item @code{print}
Prints text to output.
@item @code{format}
Formats and prints text.
@item @code{dialogue}
Displays dialogue.
@item @code{dialog}
Alias for dialogue.
@item @code{say}
Speaks dialogue text.
@item @code{input}
Gets user input.
@item @code{ask}
Asks a question with response.
@item @code{strcat}
Concatenates strings.
@item @code{strlen}
Returns string length.
@item @code{substr}
Extracts substring.
@item @code{upcase}
Converts string to uppercase.
@item @code{downcase}
Converts string to lowercase.
@item @code{numtostr}
Converts number to string.
@item @code{strtonum}
Converts string to number.
@end table

@subsection Operators

@table @asis
@item @code{+}
Addition.
@item @code{-}
Subtraction.
@item @code{*}
Multiplication.
@item @code{/}
Division.
@item @code{=}
Equality comparison.
@item @code{<>}
Inequality comparison.
@item @code{<}
Less than.
@item @code{>}
Greater than.
@item @code{<=}
Less than or equal.
@item @code{>=}
Greater than or equal.
@item @code{&} or @code{and}
Logical AND.
@item @code{|} or @code{or}
Logical OR.
@item @code{!} or @code{not}
Logical NOT.
@end table

@subsection Literal Formats

@table @asis
@item Decimal
Bare digits: @code{42}, @code{0}, @code{100}
@item Hexadecimal
@code{#x@var{hex}} or @code{0x@var{hex}} prefix: @code{#xFF} (255), @code{0x1A} (26)
@item Octal
@code{#o@var{octal}} or @code{0o@var{octal}} prefix: @code{#o77} (63), @code{0o10} (8)
@item Binary
@code{#b@var{binary}} or @code{0b@var{binary}} prefix: @code{#b1010} (10), @code{0b1111} (15)
@item DWORD
@code{d"@var{word}"} format: @code{d"SCUM"} (returns string "SCUM")
@item Strings
Double-quoted: @code{"Hello, world!"}
@end table

@subsection Delimiters

@table @asis
@item @code{(} @code{)}
Parentheses for S-expressions and grouping.
@item @code{,}
Comma separates items in lists.
@item @code{'}
Single quote denotes quoted literal.
@end table

@subsection Comments

Semicolon (;) begins a comment that continues to the end of the line:

@example
; This is a comment
(setq x 10)  ; This is also a comment
@end example

@node S-Expression Structure
@section S-Expression Structure

SCI uses S-expressions (symbolic expressions) as its primary syntax. Everything
is enclosed in parentheses, with the first element being an operator or special form.

@subsection Basic S-Expression Forms

@table @asis
@item Function call
@code{(@var{func} @var{arg1} @var{arg2} @dots{})}
@*
First element is function name, followed by arguments.

@item Special form
@code{(@var{keyword} @var{body})}
@*
Keywords like @code{if}, @code{while}, @code{setq} have special evaluation rules.

@item Nested expression
@code{(@var{op} (@var{op} a b) c)}
@*
Expressions can be nested arbitrarily deep.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(+ 10 20)
(setq score 100)
(if (> x 0) (setq positive TRUE) (setq positive FALSE))
(while (< i 10) (setq i (+ i 1)))
@end example

@node Classes and Instances
@section Classes and Instances

SCI supports object-oriented programming through classes and instances.

@subsection Class Definition

@defsyn
(class @var{name} of @var{superclass}
  (properties
    @var{prop1} @var{value1}
    @var{prop2} @var{value2})
  (method (@var{method-name} @var{params})
    @var{body})
  @dots{})
@end defsyn

Defines a class with properties and methods. The @var{superclass} specifies
the parent class for inheritance.

@subsubsection Parameters

@table @asis
@item @var{name}
Class identifier (normalized to PascalCase).
@item @var{superclass}
Parent class identifier.
@item @var{properties}
List of property name-value pairs.
@item @var{method}
Method definitions with parameters and body.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(class CPlayer of CGameActor
  (properties
    x 0
    y 0
    sprite 0
    health 100)
  (method (init theX theY theSprite)
    (= x theX)
    (= y theY)
    (= sprite theSprite))
  (method (changePos dx dy)
    (= x (+ x dx))
    (= y (+ y dy)))
)
@end example

@subsection Instance Creation

@defsyn
(instance @var{name} of @var{class}
  (properties
    @var{prop1} @var{value1}))
@end defsyn

Creates an instance of a class with optional property overrides.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(instance gPlayer of CPlayer
  (properties
    x 100
    y 200
    sprite 5))

(instance gGameState of CGameState
  (properties
    score 0
    lives 3))
@end example

@node Methods
@section Methods

Methods are functions associated with classes that operate on object instances.

@subsection Method Definition

@defsyn
(method (@var{name} @var{params})
  @var{body})
@end defsyn

Defines a method within a class. Parameters are bound to the passed arguments.

@subsubsection Parameters

@table @asis
@item @var{name}
Method identifier.
@item @var{params}
Parameter names (local variables).
@item @var{body}
S-expressions forming the method body.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(method (move dx dy)
  (= x (+ x dx))
  (= y (+ y dy))
  (self updateSprite:))

(method (getDistance other)
  (local dx dy dist)
  (= dx (- (other x:) x))
  (= dy (- (other y:) y))
  (= dist (sqrt (+ (* dx dx) (* dy dy))))
  (return dist))
@end example

@subsection Method Invocation

Methods are invoked via message passing (see @ref{Message Passing}).

@node Statements
@section Statements

@menu
* Variable Assignment::
* Procedure Definition::
* Procedure Call::
* Return Statement::
* Print Statement::
* Input Statement::
* Dialogue Statement::
@end menu

@node Variable Assignment
@subsection Variable Assignment

@defsyn
(setq @var{variable} @var{value})
@end defsyn

Assigns value to variable. The @code{=} form is also accepted for compatibility.

@subsubsection Syntax Variations

@table @asis
@item Simple assignment
@code{(setq @var{variable} @var{value})}
@*
Basic variable assignment.

@item Arithmetic assignment
@code{(setq @var{variable} (+ @var{var} @var{value}))}
@*
Assignment with arithmetic operation.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(setq gScore 0)
(setq gLivesLeft 3)
(setq gCounter (+ gCounter 1))
(setq gScore (+ gScore 10))
(setq gMessage "Hello, World!")
@end example

@subsubsection Property Access

@defsyn
(setq @var{object}:@var{property} @var{value})
@end defsyn

Accesses and assigns to object properties using the colon notation.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(setq gPlayer:x 160)
(setq gPlayer:y 100)
(setq gPlayer:sprite 5)
(setq gPlayer:visible TRUE)
@end example

@node Procedure Definition
@subsection Procedure Definition

@defsyn
(procedure (@var{name} @var{params})
  @var{body})
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(define @var{name} (@var{params})
  @var{body})
@end defsyn

Defines a procedure (function) with parameters and body. Both @code{procedure}
and @code{define} are supported.

@subsubsection Parameters

@table @asis
@item @var{name}
Procedure identifier.
@item @var{params}
Parameter names (may be empty for nullary procedures).
@item @var{body}
S-expressions forming the procedure body.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(procedure (InitializeGame)
  (= gScore 0)
  (= gLivesLeft 3)
  (= gCurrentRoom 1))

(procedure (CalculateBonus level timeLeft)
  (local bonus)
  (= bonus (* level 100))
  (return (- bonus timeLeft)))
@end example

@node Procedure Call
@subsection Procedure Call

@defsyn
(@var{procedure-name} @var{arg1} @var{arg2} @dots{})
@end defsyn

Calls a procedure with the specified arguments.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(InitializeGraphics)
(ClearScreen)
(DrawSprite gSpriteId gXPos gYPos)
(CalculateBonus gLevel gTimeLeft)
@end example

@node Return Statement
@subsection Return Statement

@defsyn
(return)
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(return @var{value})
@end defsyn

Returns from the current procedure. Optionally returns a value.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(return)
(return 0)
(return (+ score bonus))
(return (self getDistance: other))
@end example

@node Print Statement
@subsection Print Statement

@defsyn
(print @var{arg1} @var{arg2} @dots{})
@end defsyn

Prints text and optional values to output. The @code{format} function provides
additional formatting control.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(print "Hello, world!")
(print "Score: " gScore)
(print "X: " x " Y: " y)
(print "The value is: " (+ a b))
@end example

@subsubsection Format Function

@defsyn
(format @var{dest} @var{format-string} @var{args} @dots{})
@end defsyn

Formats text with printf-style placeholders. Placeholders include:
@code{%d} for decimal, @code{%s} for string, @code{%c} for character.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(format nil "Score: %d" gScore)
(format nil "Name: %s Age: %d" name age)
@end example

@node Input Statement
@subsection Input Statement

@defsyn
(input @var{prompt})
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(input @var{prompt} @var{variable})
@end defsyn

Reads user input and stores the result. If variable is provided, stores the input
to that variable; otherwise, returns the input value.

@subsubsection Parameters

@table @asis
@item @var{prompt}
String literal displayed to prompt the user.
@item @var{variable}
Optional identifier to store the input value.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(input "Enter your name: ")
(input "Enter choice: " gChoice)
(setq gPlayerName (input "Name: "))
@end example

@node Dialogue Statement
@subsection Dialogue Statement

@defsyn
(dialogue @var{character} @var{text})
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(dialogue @var{character} @var{text} @var{response1} @var{response2} @dots{})
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(say @var{character} @var{text})
@end defsyn

Displays dialogue text attributed to a character. Optional response choices
may be provided for player selection.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(dialogue "Guard" "Halt! Who goes there?")
(dialogue "Narrator" "You enter a dark cave.")
(say "Shopkeeper" "What would you like to buy?")
@end example

@node Control Flow
@section Control Flow

@menu
* Conditional Statement::
* While Loop::
* For Loop::
* Foreach Loop::
* Break and Continue::
@end menu

@node Conditional Statement
@subsection Conditional Statement: if-then-else

@defsyn
(if @var{condition}
  @var{then-form})
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(if @var{condition}
  @var{then-form}
@var{else-form})
@end defsyn

Executes @var{then-form} if condition is true (non-zero), otherwise executes
@var{else-form} if present.

@subsubsection Syntax Variations

@table @asis
@item Simple conditional
@code{(if @var{cond} @var{then})}
@*
Single form in true branch.

@item Conditional with else
@code{(if @var{cond} @var{then} @var{else})}
@*
Two-branch conditional.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(if (> gScore 1000)
    (setq gLevel (+ gLevel 1)))

(if (> gTemperature gTHOT)
    (setq gStatus "HOT")
  (elseif (> gTemperature gTCOLD)
    (setq gStatus "WARM")
  (else
    (setq gStatus "COLD")))
@end example

@node While Loop
@subsection While Loop

@defsyn
(while @var{condition}
  @var{body})
@end defsyn

Repeats body while condition is true. The condition is evaluated before
each iteration.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(= gI 1)
(while (<= gI 10)
    (Printf "Count: %d" gI)
    (= gI (+ gI 1)))
@end example

@node For Loop
@subsection For Loop

@defsyn
(for @var{var} @var{start} @var{end}
  @var{body})
@end defsyn

Iterates @var{var} from @var{start} to @var{end} (inclusive), executing body
each iteration.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(for gI 1 10
    (Printf "Number: %d" gI))

(for gCount 0 (- gMaxItems 1)
    (= (ArrayGet gItems gCount) 0))
@end example

@node Foreach Loop
@subsection Foreach Loop

@defsyn
(foreach @var{element} @var{collection}
  @var{body})
@end defsyn

Iterates over each element in a collection, executing body with element bound
to the current item.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(foreach gElem gList
    (Printf "%s" gElem))
@end example

@node Break and Continue
@subsection Break and Continue

@subsubsection Break

@defsyn
(break)
@end defsyn

Exits the innermost enclosing loop immediately.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(= gI 1)
(while (<= gI 100)
    (if (= (ListGet gArray gI) gTARGET_VALUE)
        (progn
          (Printf "Found at index: %d" gI)
          (break)))
    (= gI (+ gI 1)))
@end example

@subsubsection Continue

@defsyn
(continue)
@end defsyn

Skips the remainder of the current loop iteration.

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(= gI 1)
(while (<= gI 100)
    (if (< (ListGet gArray gI) 0)
        (continue))
    ; Process non-negative values
    (= gI (+ gI 1)))
@end example

@node Arithmetic Operations
@section Arithmetic Operations

@menu
* Basic Arithmetic::
* Division and Multiplication::
* Complex Expressions::
@end menu

@node Basic Arithmetic
@subsection Basic Arithmetic

@defsyn
(+ @var{expr} @var{expr})
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(- @var{expr} @var{expr})
@end defsyn

Addition (+) produces the sum of two operands.
Subtraction (-) produces the difference (left minus right).

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(= gScore (+ gScore 10))
(= gLivesLeft (- gLivesLeft 1))
(= gTotal (+ gWidth gHeight))
(= gFinalPrice (- gPrice gDiscount))
@end example

@node Division and Multiplication
@subsection Division and Multiplication

@defsyn
(* @var{expr} @var{expr})
@end defsyn

@defsyn
(/ @var{expr} @var{expr})
@end defsyn

Multiplication (*) produces the product of two operands.
Division (/) produces the quotient (integer division).

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(= gResult (* gValue 4))
(= gResult (/ gValue 2))
(= gAverage (/ (+ gSum1 gSum2 gSum3) 3))
@end example

@node Complex Expressions
@subsection Complex Expressions

@example
(= gTotal (+ (* gBaseSalary 12) gBonus (- gDeductions)))
(= gAverage (/ (+ gSum1 gSum2 gSum3) 3.0))
(= gDistance (sqrt (+ (sqr (- gX2 gX1)) (sqr (- gY2 gY1)))))
@end example

@node String Operations
@section String Operations

SCI provides built-in string manipulation functions.

@table @asis
@item @code{(strcat @var{str1} @var{str2} @dots{})}
Concatenates strings. Returns the combined string.

@item @code{(strlen @var{string})}
Returns the length of string as an integer.

@item @code{(substr @var{string} @var{start} @var{length})}
Extracts substring from string starting at start (0-indexed) for length characters.

@item @code{(upcase @var{string})}
Returns string converted to uppercase.

@item @code{(downcase @var{string})}
Returns string converted to lowercase.

@item @code{(numtostr @var{number})}
Converts number to string representation.

@item @code{(strtonum @var{string})}
Converts string to number.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(setq gFullName (strcat gFirstName " " gLastName))
(setq gNameLength (strlen gPlayerName))
(setq gInitials (substr gPlayerName 0 3))
(setq gUpperName (upcase gPlayerName))
(setq gScoreStr (numtostr gScore))
(setq gNumber (strtonum "42"))
@end example

@node Input and Output
@section Input and Output

The SCI frontend provides I/O commands for user interaction:

@table @asis
@item @code{(print @var{args} @dots{})}
Display text (see @ref{Print Statement})

@item @code{(input @var{prompt} @var{var})}
Read user input (see @ref{Input Statement})

@item @code{(dialogue @var{char} @var{text})}
Display dialogue (see @ref{Dialogue Statement})
@end table

@node Message Passing
@section Message Passing

SCI uses message passing for object-oriented programming. The @code{send} construct
invokes methods on objects.

@defsyn
(send @var{object} '@var{method} @var{arg1} @var{arg2} @dots{})
@end defsyn

Sends a message to an object, invoking the specified method with the provided arguments.

@subsubsection Parameters

@table @asis
@item @var{object}
The target object instance.
@item @var{method}
The method name (quoted with single quote).
@item @var{argN}
Arguments to pass to the method.
@end table

@subsubsection Examples

@example
(send gPlayer 'changePos 5 10)
(send gScoreDisplay 'update gScore)
(= gGameOver (send gGameState 'isGameOver))
(send gActor 'setX: (+ (gActor 'x:) dx))
@end example

@subsubsection Superclass Access

The @code{super} construct calls the parent class implementation:

@example
(method (init)
    (super init:)
    (= health 100))
@end example

@subsubsection Self Reference

The @code{self} construct refers to the current object instance:

@example
(method (move dx dy)
    (= x (+ x dx))
    (= y (+ y dy))
    (self updateSprite:))
@end example

@node Unsupported Features
@section Unsupported Features

The following SCI features are not supported in this EIGHTBOL release:

@table @asis
@item File I/O operations
@code{Fopen}, @code{Fread}, @code{Fwrite}, @code{Fclose} are not implemented.

@item Graphics commands
@code{DrawPic}, @code{Animate}, @code{ShowPic} are not implemented.

@item Hardware-specific features
Joystick, mouse, and extended keyboard beyond basic input are not supported.

@item Extended memory handling
Unless emulated by the target platform.

@item Multithreading or concurrent execution
Not supported.

@item Exception handling
Unless via external interface.

@item Pointer arithmetic and manual memory management
Not supported.

@item Preprocessor directives
@code{#define}, @code{#ifdef} are not implemented.

@item Multiple inheritance
Not supported unless using external library.

@item Sound and music commands
Unless using external library.
@end table

@node Example Programs
@section Example Programs

@subsubsection Game State Machine

@example
; Initialize game
(define InitializeGame ()
    (= gScore 0)
    (= gLivesLeft 3)
    (= gCurrentRoom 1)
    (= gGameOver FALSE))

; Main game loop
(procedure (GameLoop)
    (while (not gGameOver)
        (ProcessInput)
        (UpdateGame)
        (RenderDisplay)
        (if (<= gLivesLeft 0)
            (= gGameOver TRUE)))
    (Print "Game Over!")
    (Print "Final Score: " gScore))
@end example

@subsubsection Player Class

@example
(class CPlayer of CGameActor
  (properties
    x 100
    y 100
    sprite 0
    health 100
    inventorySize 10)

  (method (init theX theY theSprite)
    (= x theX)
    (= y theY)
    (= sprite theSprite)
    (= health 100))

  (method (changePos dx dy)
    (= x (+ x dx))
    (= y (+ y dy))
    (self updateSprite:))

  (method (takeDamage amount)
    (= health (- health amount))
    (if (<= health 0)
        (self die:)))

  (method (heal amount)
    (= health (+ health amount))
    (if (> health 100)
        (= health 100))))
@end example

@subsubsection Dialogue System

@example
; Dialogue manager
(class CDialogueManager of CObject
  (properties
    currentNpc NULL
    responses NULL)

  (method (init)
    (= responses (CreateArray 10)))

  (method (show character text)
    (= currentNpc character)
    (dialogue character text))

  (method (ask character text response1 response2)
    (dialogue character text response1 response2)
    (input "Your choice: " gDialogueChoice)
    (return gDialogueChoice)))

; Usage
(instance gDialogue of CDialogueManager
  (properties))

(setq gChoice (gDialogue 'ask: "Shopkeeper"
    "What would you like to buy?" "Sword" "Leave"))
@end example
